  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The electric field due to a large uniformly charged non-conducting sheet is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#963;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>. It is independent of the distance from the sheet. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#963;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"
